Some stuff is so much fun you lose track of the
point of the game entirely.

Just now, Wobble Bat, orcish female wizard
Thaumaturge, is exporing two levels below Mines
Town, accompanied by her pets:

Barkless the dog
Purrball III the large cat
Da Wiz the gnomish wizard
Lord Over the gnomish lord
Whinney I the war horse
Mines Town Howler the large dog
Biggie the stone giant
Hugie the stone giant

Progress is a mass of confusion, but a magic whistle
sure helps a lot. One toot at the approach of the
foes, and even finding their death dropped goodies
is a challenge.

Having cleaned out _five_ Mines Town shops, plus
_three_ shops at DLVL 2, 3, and 4, and donated all
to the cross-aligned altar's priestess, Wobble Bat
is running around naked except for her birth-cloak,
and still at AC -1. This has taken a while, though,
and at 13,410 turns into the game, the charm monster
spell, from a birth-spellbook long ago abandoned
higher up in some stash, has only a short remaining
lifetime.

Got to live for the moment, 'cause dying by the YASD
is a given.

